er="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129734025.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/why-greenland-has-almost-no-trees-and-what-makes-it-so-unusual-the-reason-will-shock-you/articleshow/129734025.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/why-greenland-has-almost-no-trees-and-what-makes-it-so-unusual-the-reason-will-shock-you/articleshow/129734025.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-23T01:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129734084,imgsize-104266.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Who knows surprise better than Japan?’ Trump’s Pearl Harbor remark sparks unease in Tokyo during Iran war statement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129735481.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[President Trump's Pearl Harbor remark to justify his Iran attack sparked outrage in Japan. Critics called his comments ignorant and disrespectful, questioning Japan's equal partnership status. While Prime Minister Takaichi remained silent, many felt she should have protested the historical insensitivity and the war itself, highlighting ongoing debates about Japan's wartime role.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-knows-surprise-better-than-japan-trumps-pearl-harbor-remark-sparks-unease-in-tokyo-during-iran-war-statement/articleshow/129735481.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/who-knows-surprise-better-than-japan-trumps-pearl-harbor-remark-sparks-unease-in-tokyo-during-iran-war-statement/articleshow/129735481.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-03-22T22:53:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http: